From: Ershad Kunnakkadan <ershad92@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:41:45 +0530
Subject: Decode status replies by payload size, not total reply size
Origin: https://github.com/mounaiban/captdriver/commit/258a161d084ba1167e573c9444dc588e1ce1ef15
Forwarded: https://github.com/mounaiban/captdriver/pull/55
Last-Update: 2026-11-09

capt_sendrecv() reports the reply size including the 4-byte header but
copies only the payload into the caller's buffer. download_status()
passed that total to decode_status(), so an 8-byte basic status reply
(A0 E0) was decoded as 12 bytes: status[1] came from leftovers in
capt_iobuf and the page counters from uninitialized stack.

On macOS/arm64 the stack held zeros, so after the page uploaded the
counters reset, CAPT_FIRE went out for page 0 and the job never
printed. Pass the payload size and only decode fields the reply
actually contains; basic status now updates status[0] and buf_level,
leaving the counters at their last extended-status values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/capt-status.c | 13 +++++++------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/capt-status.c b/src/capt-status.c
index b5465a6..9bd2593 100644
--- a/src/capt-status.c
+++ b/src/capt-status.c
@@ -56,15 +56,15 @@ static void decode_status(const uint8_t *s, size_t size)
 {
 	status.status[0] = WORD(s[0], s[1]);
 
-	if (size <= 2)
-		return;
-
-	if (size > 8)
+	if (size > 4)
 		status.buf_level = s[4];  /* CAPT_BSTAT_BUF_LO / CAPT_XSTAT_BUF_LO */
 
+	if (size < 10)
+		return;
+
 	status.status[1] = WORD(s[8], s[9]);
 
-	if (size <= 10)
+	if (size < 40)
 		return;
 
 	status.aux            = s[CAPT_XSTAT_AUX];    /* Aux auxiliary engine status */
@@ -93,7 +93,8 @@ static void download_status(uint16_t cmd)
 	uint8_t buf[0x10000];
 	size_t size = sizeof(buf);
 	capt_sendrecv(cmd, NULL, 0, buf, &size);
-	decode_status(buf, size);
+	/* size counts the 4-byte reply header, but only the payload lands in buf */
+	decode_status(buf, size - 4);
 }
 
 void capt_init_status(void)
